<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baoji</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baoji is a city in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wei-river">Wei River</a> at the western end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guanzhong">Guanzhong</a> plain. The area was an early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the Zhou, whose ancestral plain of Zhouyuan lies within its territory, and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-qin">State of Qin</a>. Many Western Zhou bronzes have been found there, and the city has a museum devoted to them.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baoji.jpg" alt="Baoji" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PastaPastaRavioli · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BaojiSkyline.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
